cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this design or its tools, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TD-µT: reprogrammable dual-engine protocol emulator ASIC"
abstract: >-
  A reprogrammable protocol emulator ASIC for Tiny Tapeout on IHP CMOS5L: two
  microcode engines (physical layer and protocol layer) coupled by a
  backpressured FIFO, with a generic hardware bit pipe (NRZI, bit stuffing,
  CRC) and a glitch filter. UART, SPI, I2C and USB low-speed receive run as
  programs loaded over the pins. RTL in Hardcaml; assembler and loader in Axiom.
authors:
  - family-names: Templet
    given-names: Jessica
repository-code: "https://github.com/JessicaTemplet/td-ut-protocol-emulator"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - ASIC
  - Tiny Tapeout
  - IHP CMOS5L
  - Hardcaml
  - Axiom
  - protocol emulator
  - USB
references:
  - type: software
    title: Axiom
    abstract: "The language the assembler and program loader (tools/tdasm) is written in."
    authors:
      - family-names: Paige
        given-names: Chris
    repository-code: "https://github.com/chrispaig3/Axiom"
    version: "0.7.8"
  - type: software
    title: Hardcaml
    abstract: "The hardware description library the RTL is written in."
    authors:
